</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p2.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:173%;">Appendix</span></p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix S1 </span>Theoretical Explanation of Efficiency Gains</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">I now further investigate why the SRI framework can yield efficiency gains compared to existing methods in general. To compare Surrogate Representation Inference (SRI) with the existing bias-correction approach, I first define each semiparametric model and the corresponding tangent space. Let <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{SRI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{SRI}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a semiparametric model of Surrogate Representation Inference (SRI) and <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{PPI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{PPI}}</annotation></semantics></math> be that of the existing bias-correction methodology. Then, the observed data for each semiparametric model, denoted as <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{\text{SRI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\text{SRI}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{\text{PPI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\text{PPI}}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively, are written as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex38.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Surrogate Representation Inference:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O_{\text{SRI}}=\{T_{i},\bm{f}(\mathbf{Y}_{i}),\mathbf{Z}_{i},S_{i},G_{S_{i}}(\tilde{L}_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O_{\text{SRI}}=\{T_{i},\bm{f}(\mathbf{Y}_{i}),\mathbf{Z}_{i},S_{i},G_{S_{i}}(\tilde{L}_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex39.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Existing Methods:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O_{\text{PPI}}=\{T_{i},\bm{h}(\mathbf{Y}_{i}),\mathbf{Z}_{i},S_{i},G_{S_{i}}(\tilde{L}_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O_{\text{PPI}}=\{T_{i},\bm{h}(\mathbf{Y}_{i}),\mathbf{Z}_{i},S_{i},G_{S_{i}}(\tilde{L}_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the predictor of interest, <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of control variables, <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the human annotation, <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the indicator variable for whether the human annotation <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is observed, <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{S_{i}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{S_{i}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the coarsening operator that outputs the input when <math id="A1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and outputs the empty set when <math id="A1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{f}}(\bm{Y}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{f}}(\bm{Y}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is the surrogate representation satisfying the independence constraint <math id="A1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\ \tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}\ \mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\ \tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{h}(\bm{Y}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{h}(\bm{Y}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is the machine learning-based proxy. For the sake of analytical simplicity, assume that <math id="A1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim(\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i}))=\dim(\bm{h}(\bm{Y}_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim(\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i}))=\dim(\bm{h}(\bm{Y}_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be assumed without loss of generality since <math id="A1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{L}_{i}=L_{i}=g_{L}(\bm{Y}_{i})\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{L}_{i}=L_{i}=g_{L}(\bm{Y}_{i})\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> trivially satisfies the independence constraint (i.e., statistical surrogacy condition). Then, without any constraints on machine learning predictions, <math id="A1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{SRI}}\subseteq\mathcal{M}_{\text{PPI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{SRI}}\subseteq\mathcal{M}_{\text{PPI}}</annotation></semantics></math>, since any factorization under <math id="A1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{SRI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{SRI}}</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to <math id="A1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{PPI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{PPI}}</annotation></semantics></math>. As a result, the tangent space of Surrogate Representation Inference, denoted as <math id="A1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is a linear subspace of that of the existing method <math id="A1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the entire Hilbert space due to no restrictions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In semiparametric statistics, the model’s efficiency is often evaluated in terms of the <em id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">semiparametric efficiency bound</em>, which is the analogue of the Cramér-Rao lower bound for the semiparametric problem and no semiparametric estimators can have an asymptotic variance smaller than this bound (e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bickel et al., 1993</a>; <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Newey, 1990</a>; <a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vaart, 1998</a>; <a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tsiatis, 2006</a></cite>). To see the efficiency gains of the independence constraint, we compare the efficiency bounds for the two different methods. Mathematically, they are given by</p>
<table id="A1.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex40.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Surrogate Representation Inference:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex41.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Existing Methods:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{i}=\{T_{i},\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{i}=\{T_{i},\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of variables required to consider the score, <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(O_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(O_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is the score function, and <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pi(\cdot\mid\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi(\cdot\mid\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the projection operator (note that we can remove <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> when considering the score since it is a deterministic function of <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>). As <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}}\subseteq\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}}\subseteq\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})}_{\text{Efficient Score for SRI}}=\underbrace{S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})}_{\text{Efficient Score for PPI}}+\underbrace{\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})}_{:=\Delta\ (\text{residual term)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>Efficient Score for SRI</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>Efficient Score for PPI</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.410em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>residual term)</mtext><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})}_{\text{Efficient Score for SRI}}=\underbrace{S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})}_{\text{Efficient Score for PPI}}+\underbrace{\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})}_{:=\Delta\ (\text{residual term)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where the residual term <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is orthogonal to the efficient score for PPI. As a result, since <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\in\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\in\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the efficient score belongs to the orthogonal complement of the tangent space,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>SRI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{SRI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})+\Delta\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})+\Delta\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})+\Delta\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})+\Delta\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]+\mathbb{E}[\Delta\Delta^{\top}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]+\mathbb{E}[\Delta\Delta^{\top}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\succeq\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\succeq\mathbb{E}\biggl[\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)\biggl(S(O_{i})-\Pi(S(O_{i})\mid\mathcal{T}_{\text{PPI}})\biggr)^{\top}\biggr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where the third equality is by the orthogonality of the residual term to the efficient score that lies in the orthocomplement of the tangent space. Therefore, as most of the existing literature on the bias-correction estimator works on the semiparametric model <math id="A1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{PPI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>PPI</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{PPI}}</annotation></semantics></math>, regardless of the form of the estimators, without imposing any additional restrictions, such as parametric models, SRI always has a lower semiparametric efficiency bound and the proposed estimator in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> attains this bound.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">From this theoretical analysis, it is expected that when the machine learning predictions already achieve high accuracy, there should not be much efficiency gain in reality. This is because our efficiency gains come from the fact that the machine learning predictions do not necessarily satisfy the independence constraint, but if they are almost accurate, as they almost satisfy the independence constraint, there is no reason to expect that the residual term <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> will become large. I confirm this conjecture in the application section (Section <a href="#S5" title="5 Empirical Application ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) and the simulation section (Section <a href="#A3" title="Appendix S3 Simulation Studies ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix S2 </span>Theoretical Results</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">S2.1 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Identification under Perfect Annotations) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (Identification of Target Parameter)</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">As <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;\bm{Y}_{i}\;\mid\;\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;\bm{Y}_{i}\;\mid\;\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (by Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4 (Sufficiency of Representation for Texts) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), the use of Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (True Coding Rule) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;L_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;L_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now, notice that Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Human Annotation Sampling) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> indicates the marginal independence <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the deterministic function of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Human Annotation Sampling) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we can claim</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{Y}_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;S_{i}\;\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{Y}_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;S_{i}\;\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">because</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y},S_{i}=s\mid\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y},S_{i}=s\mid\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y},S_{i}=s,\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)}{\mathbb{P}(\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y},S_{i}=s,\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)}{\mathbb{P}(\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y},\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)\;\mathbb{P}(S_{i}=s)}{\mathbb{P}(\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y},\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)\;\mathbb{P}(S_{i}=s)}{\mathbb{P}(\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y}\mid\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)\;\mathbb{P}(S_{i}=s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y}\mid\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)\;\mathbb{P}(S_{i}=s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y}\mid\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)\;\mathbb{P}(S_{i}=s\mid\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\bm{Y}_{i}=\bm{y}\mid\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)\;\mathbb{P}(S_{i}=s\mid\bm{W}_{i}\in A,\bm{Z}_{i}\in B)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">for any <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> and any pair of Borel sets <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B</annotation></semantics></math>. In the above transformation, we apply Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Human Annotation Sampling) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and the fact that <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the deterministic function of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in the second line, and the final line is because <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\bm{W}_{i},,\bm{Z}_{i}\}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bm{W}_{i},,\bm{Z}_{i}\}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. By applying Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (True Coding Rule) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;S_{i}\;\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;S_{i}\;\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Psi_{t}:=\mathbb{E}\biggl[\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid T_{i}=t,\bm{Z}_{i}]\biggr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Psi_{t}:=\mathbb{E}\biggl[\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid T_{i}=t,\bm{Z}_{i}]\biggr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid T_{i}=t,\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid T_{i}=t,\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i}]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[L_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">where we use the law of iterated expectation in the first line, Equation <a href="#A2.E1" title="In Proof. ‣ S2.1 Proof of Proposition (Identification of Target Parameter) ‣ Appendix S2 Theoretical Results ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S1</span></a>
in the second line, and Equation <a href="#A2.E3" title="In Proof. ‣ S2.1 Proof of Proposition (Identification of Target Parameter) ‣ Appendix S2 Theoretical Results ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S3</span></a> in the third line, and Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Perfect Annotations) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> in the last line. As <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is observed under <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> by definition, we can estimate both <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\bm{W}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)</annotation></semantics></math> from the data.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we show that <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}</annotation></semantics></math> does not need to be unique. Notice that the formula above is equivalent to</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Psi_{t}=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒇</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Psi_{t}=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniquely specified by researchers but <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}</annotation></semantics></math> is estimated from data and might not be unique. Suppose that there exists another <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}^{\prime}=\bm{f}^{\prime}(\bm{Y}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}^{\prime}=\bm{f}^{\prime}(\bm{Y}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{W}^{\prime},\bm{Z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{W}^{\prime},\bm{Z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Psi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Psi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex56.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}^{\prime}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}^{\prime}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}^{\prime}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}^{\prime}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]dF(\bm{Y}_{i}\mid\bm{Z}_{i},T_{i}=t)dF(\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
