<p id="A2.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we use <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;\tilde{L}_{i}\;\mid\bm{f}^{\prime}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}_{i}\;\mbox{$\perp\!\!\!\perp$}\;\tilde{L}_{i}\;\mid\bm{f}^{\prime}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> in the second line. This is because</span></p>
