<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">for any <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\in\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\in\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, and any pair of Borel sets <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B</annotation></semantics></math>. In the above transformation, we use Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4 (Sufficiency of Representation for Texts) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> for the fourth line. Hence, we can say that the different <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{f}</annotation></semantics></math> still leads to the same identification formula.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">S2.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Efficient Influence Function) ‣ 3.2 Estimation and inference ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (Efficient Influence Function)</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Here, we use the technique called point-mass contamination approach <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kennedy,, 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hines et al.,, 2022</a>)</cite>. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hines et al., (2022)</a></cite>, we assume that <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> are continuous only for the notational convenience, but as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hines et al., (2022)</a></cite> discussed, the entire proof works with discrete variables or a mix of discrete and continuous variables.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> be a true data distribution and <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{t}(\mathcal{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{t}(\mathcal{P})</annotation></semantics></math> be an estimand under <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=t\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=t\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and true data distribution <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. That is,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Psi_{t}(\mathcal{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Psi_{t}(\mathcal{P})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mu_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}),\bm{z})f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mu_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}),\bm{z})f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i})=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i})=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{W}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> is the expectation operator under the distribution <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathcal{P}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathcal{P}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the PDF under the true distribution <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, consider the parametric submodel <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}=(1-\epsilon)\mathcal{P}+\epsilon\tilde{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}=(1-\epsilon)\mathcal{P}+\epsilon\tilde{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the point mass at <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{t},\tilde{\bm{y}},\tilde{l},\tilde{\bm{z}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>l</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{t},\tilde{\bm{y}},\tilde{l},\tilde{\bm{z}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the influence of perturbation in the direction of <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\Psi_{t}(\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon})\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}=\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mu_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y}),\bm{z})f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\Psi_{t}(\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon})\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}=\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\mu_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y}),\bm{z})f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i})=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i})=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}[\tilde{L}_{i}\mid\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i},S_{i}=1]</annotation></semantics></math> is the outcome model under <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> is the expectation operator under <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the CDF under <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> can be regarded as a composite function, for the sake of simplicity, let <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=\mu_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=\mu_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=\mu_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒇</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i},\bm{Z}_{i})=\mu_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{f}_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, under the regularity condition, we can switch the derivative and integrals, and thus the chain rule yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}m_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})\,f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}m_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})\,f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\quad=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\frac{d}{d\epsilon}m_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}\,f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\quad=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\frac{d}{d\epsilon}m_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}\,f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad+\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}m_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\,f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad+\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}m_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\,f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad+\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}m_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\,f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{z})\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}d\bm{y}d\bm{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad+\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}m_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)\frac{d}{d\epsilon}\,f_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{z})\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}d\bm{y}d\bm{z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">For the first component,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\frac{d}{d\epsilon}m_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}\,f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\int_{\mathcal{Y}}\frac{d}{d\epsilon}m_{\mathcal{P}_{\epsilon}}(\bm{y},\bm{z})\biggl|_{\epsilon=0}\,f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{y}\mid\bm{z},T_{i}=t)f_{\mathcal{P}}(\bm{z})d\bm{y}d\bm{z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
