</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the third line is by triangular inequality, the fourth line is by Cauchy-Schwartz inequality, and the last line is by <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[|\tilde{L}_{i}|^{2}]^{\frac{1}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[|\tilde{L}_{i}|^{2}]^{\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption5" title="Assumption 5 (Regularity Conditions) ‣ 3.2 Estimation and inference ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{23}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>23</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{23}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

