</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second line is by the law of iterated expectation and the third line is by Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4 (Sufficiency of Representation for Texts) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, by combining all the terms, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

