<tbody id="A2.Ex274"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex274.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbbm{1}\{S_{i}=1\}}{\mathbb{P}(S_{i}=1)}\cdot\mathbb{E}\biggl[\frac{\rho_{t}(\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i})}{\pi_{t}(\bm{Z}_{i})}\biggl\{\mathbbm{1}\{L_{i}=c\}-\mathbbm{1}\{L_{i}=c\}\biggr\}\biggr]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>S</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒀</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbbm{1}\{S_{i}=1\}}{\mathbb{P}(S_{i}=1)}\cdot\mathbb{E}\biggl[\frac{\rho_{t}(\bm{f}(\bm{Y}_{i}),\bm{Z}_{i})}{\pi_{t}(\bm{Z}_{i})}\biggl\{\mathbbm{1}\{L_{i}=c\}-\mathbbm{1}\{L_{i}=c\}\biggr\}\biggr]=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the third line is by the law of iterated expectation,
the sixth line is by Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption7" title="Assumption 7 (Noisy Human Annotations) ‣ 4.1 Assumptions and nonparametric identification ‣ 4 The Proposed Methodology with Noisy Human Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>,
and the last line is by the property of the surrogate outcomes and Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (True Coding Rule) ‣ 3.1 Assumptions, quantity of interest, and nonparametric identification ‣ 3 The Proposed Methodology with Perfect Annotations ‣ Surrogate Representation Inference for Noisy Text and Image Annotations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
